  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Mulliganed a 7-card hand with 4 lands and a reasonable white curve (Turn 3 Celestial Enforcer, Turn 4 Basri's Acolyte + Angelic Ascension as removal). While the hand lacks green mana in what appears to be a GW deck, the white cards provide a functional game plan and natural draws should find green sources.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to mulligan to 6 cards",
      "better_line": "Keep the 7-card hand. It has a solid curve with 3 playable white spells and 4 lands. Drawing into green sources is likely given 33 cards remaining in library. Mulliganing to 6 risks a worse hand with no guarantee of green mana.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 2,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Played Gaea's Protector instead of using Savage Punch to kill Speaker of the Heavens, the engine generating 4/4 Angel tokens every turn. Each turn Speaker survives produces another 4/4 flyer, rapidly making the board unwinnable. With Ferocious active (Rhonas is power 5), Savage Punch would give Rhonas +2/+2 and let it fight and kill Speaker easily.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Gaea's Protector for 4 mana, deploying a 4/2 body but leaving Speaker of the Heavens alive to generate another Angel token next turn.",
      "better_line": "Cast Savage Punch (2 mana) targeting Rhonas to fight Speaker of the Heavens, killing the Angel-generating engine immediately. This leaves 2 mana open for Rhonas's pump ability if needed, and Gaea's Protector can be deployed next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 79,
      "player": "MiniMx Grudge",
      "decision_index": 42,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3P Coach is at exactly 27 life — the threshold for Speaker of the Heavens to create 4/4 Angel tokens (need 27+ with starting life 20). Taking 5 from Rhonas drops them to 22, losing the Speaker activation ability which is their primary win condition engine. Blocking with Brightmare (2/3) would save 5 life and preserve the threshold, at the cost of losing a 2/3 to Rhonas's deathtouch — a very favorable trade in context.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to block Rhonas the Indomitable, taking 5 damage and dropping to 22 life (below Speaker threshold).",
      "better_line": "Block Rhonas with Brightmare (2/3) to prevent 5 damage and maintain the 27+ life threshold needed for Speaker of the Heavens to keep generating 4/4 Angel tokens.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 92,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 47,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Held back Brightmare from attacking when the opponent had no available blockers (Rhonas tapped, Gaea's Protector sick). This left 2 free damage on the table, reducing the attack from 9 to 7 damage.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only Angel Token (5/5) and Speaker of the Heavens (2/2) for 7 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack with all three available creatures (Angel Token, Speaker of the Heavens, and Brightmare) for 9 total damage since the opponent has zero available blockers. The 2/3 Brightmare provides minimal defensive value against the opponent's 5/5 and 4/2 threats.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 113,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 58,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Chose Angelic Edict over Baneslayer Angel. While exiling Rhonas (indestructible, deathtouch) is a strong play, casting Baneslayer Angel creates an overwhelming air clock: two 5/5 flyers threaten 10 damage next turn against an opponent at 13 life with no flyers. The opponent's board is fully tapped and can't interact this turn. Baneslayer's lifelink also cushions any counterattack. The Edict can be cast next turn when the mana is available again.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Angelic Edict to exile an opponent's creature (likely Rhonas)",
      "better_line": "Cast Baneslayer Angel to create a 2-turn lethal clock in the air (10 flying damage per turn vs opponent at 13 life) with lifelink to buffer against counterattacks. Save Angelic Edict for next turn if needed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 146,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 72,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 4 life facing a 5/5 flying Angel token (plus two 2/3s), casting Rampaging Growth enables an attack this turn but the 4/3 reach land-creature expires at end of turn, leaving no way to block the Angel next turn. Opponent swings for 9+ in the air and on ground, which is lethal. Savage Punch with Ferocious (Rhonas becomes 7/7, indestructible) kills the Angel permanently, and then Rhonas can block ground threats next turn to survive.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Rampaging Growth to create a temporary 4/3 reach/haste attacker and enable Rhonas to attack.",
      "better_line": "Cast Savage Punch targeting Rhonas and the Angel Token 5/5. Rhonas gets +2/+2 from Ferocious, fights as a 7/5 indestructible, kills the Angel. Then play a land and pass. Next turn, block ground threats with indestructible Rhonas and survive.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 167,
      "player": "MiniMx Grudge",
      "decision_index": 81,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 4 life facing a 5/5 flying Angel Token that will attack for lethal next turn, the player passed instead of casting Savage Punch to kill it. Rhonas the Indomitable (indestructible, 5/5) can fight the Angel Token via Savage Punch, getting +2/+2 from Ferocious to become 7/5 with deathtouch, easily destroying the Angel while surviving due to indestructible. Without removing the Angel, the opponent attacks for lethal in the air next turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn without casting Savage Punch",
      "better_line": "Cast Savage Punch targeting Rhonas the Indomitable to fight the Angel Token 5/5. With Ferocious, Rhonas becomes 7/5 with deathtouch and indestructible, killing the Angel and surviving. This removes the only lethal flying threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 188,
      "player": "MiniMx Grudge",
      "decision_index": 92,
    }
  ],
